# Everything in this repository is written with LF endings, and has to stay
# that way in the working tree - not only inside the repository.
#
# Windows checks out with core.autocrlf by default, which rewrites text files
# to CRLF. gofmt then reports every single .go file as unformatted, because
# reformatting them means putting the endings back; `./scripts/check.sh`
# therefore fails before it runs one test - in CI on windows-latest and on a
# contributor's Windows machine alike, pre-push hook included.
#
# text=auto leaves anything git detects as binary alone, so the screenshots
# and the recordings are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These are executed by a shell, where a trailing CR is a syntax error rather
# than a diff: spelled out so the reason survives a change to the rule above.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
